# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# NOTE: these strings are sourced by bash, so they MUST be free of backticks and the dollar sign (they
# trigger command/parameter substitution). Use plain quotes and the word 'cap' instead.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_resolve_fanout_bound.py" "RESOLVE FANOUT BOUND GATE: PASS" "resolve fan-out bound (cross-file N-squared DoS cap)" "import resolution fan-out is BOUNDED: the recall-biased bare-basename fan-out (a bare import like 'import util' resolves to EVERY same-basename util.py) was UNCAPPED across files, so a repo with N same-named files + N importers produced N-squared imports edges (measured 50->2,500, 200->40,000, 500->250,000 = 17.9 MB payload; the per-FILE edge cap runs BEFORE resolution so it never bounds this cross-file fan-out). _MAX_BARE_FANOUT (=8) caps the DEGREE: a bare basename resolving to MORE than 8 distinct files is low-precision wallpaper (an import that could mean any of 9+ files is not a confident single coupling) so the over-cap fan-out is DROPPED (lose noise, not signal). RECALL-SAFE: 1-8 candidates still fan out exactly as before; dotted/multi-segment/relative imports are never capped (already precise). Proven: (1) BOUNDED -- the N-same-basename adversarial repo resolved edges are at most N times cap, not N-squared; (2) NORMAL UNCHANGED -- 1/3/exactly-cap candidates still fully fan out (recall preserved); (3) PRECISE DROP -- only the over-cap BARE import drops to inert, multi-segment dotted imports resolve to their one target. Content-free (paths + module names only), never-crash, offline (no DB)." "import resolution fan-out is bounded by N times cap (cross-file N-squared blow-up closed), normal 1..cap fan-out preserved (recall-safe), only the over-cap ambiguous bare basename dropped to inert; content-free, offline" 16
